---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "About FloatJet | Tools & Resources for Remote Professionals";
const description =
  "Learn about FloatJet's mission to help remote workers and digital nomads find the best tools, software, and strategies to work efficiently from anywhere.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="container mx-auto px-4 pt-28 md:pt-36 pb-16 md:pb-20">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Hero Section -->
      <div class="text-center mb-14">
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Hi, we are floatjet</p>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-4xl md:text-6xl tracking-[-0.04em] leading-[0.95] text-ink text-balance mb-5">About FloatJet</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-ink/85">
          Real tools tested by someone who actually works remotely.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Story Section -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4">Why This Exists</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/85 text-lg leading-relaxed">
          Been doing the remote thing since around 2019. Lisbon for a while, then Bali, bunch of random Airbnbs in between.
          Coworking spaces that promised "blazing fast WiFi". Spoiler, it never was. And every time I needed a new tool?
          Some project management app or VPN or whatever? Hours down the drain reading reviews that all said the same stuff.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-4">
          "Best for professionals." Okay but what does that even mean.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-4">
          Started testing stuff myself instead. Wrote down what worked, what was trash, what looked great until you
          actually used it for more than three days.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 text-lg leading-relaxed mt-4">
          That became this site. No content team. No one getting paid to say nice things. Just notes from years of
          actually doing the remote thing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Who This Is For Section -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4">Who This Is For</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="sticker rounded-[22px] p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Remote Workers</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft">
              Maybe you've got an actual home office. Maybe it's a corner of your kitchen. Doesn't matter.I write about
              the gear and apps that make WFH less annoying. Skip the paralysis of comparing 47 options.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="sticker rounded-[22px] p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Digital Nomads</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft">
              The fun stuff like VPNs that work when you're in countries that block everything. Banks that won't freeze
              your card the second you cross a border. Laptop bags that don't fall apart after six months.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="sticker rounded-[22px] p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Freelancers</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft">
              Already juggling a hundred things. Don't need to also research invoicing apps for three hours. I test
              them, tell you what's good, you move on with your life.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="sticker rounded-[22px] p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink mb-2">Remote Teams</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft">
              Slack but cheaper? Something that's not Zoom? Project management that people might actually use? Yeah, I
              cover that. Distributed work is hard enough without bad tools making it worse.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- How I Test Section -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4">How I Actually Test This Stuff</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Not by skimming the marketing page and rewording it. Actual process:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="relative pl-12"><span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-ink bg-sun font-display text-sm font-bold" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
            <p class="text-ink font-bold">Weeks of real use, not a quick demo.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-soft mt-1">I'm using these tools on actual client work. Deadlines. Stress. The whole thing.
              When a VPN craps out during a presentation, that goes in the review. When an app seems great day one but
              gets annoying by day ten, you'll hear about it.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="relative pl-12"><span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-ink bg-sun font-display text-sm font-bold" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
            <p class="text-ink font-bold">The bad stuff doesn't get hidden.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-soft mt-1">Look. Everything has problems. Could be a small thing you can live with, could be
              a total dealbreaker. Either way it goes in the review. Not trying to sell you anything here. If something
              wasted my time, hopefully telling you saves you from the same headache.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="relative pl-12"><span class="absolute left-0 top-0 flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-[1.5px] border-ink bg-sun font-display text-sm font-bold" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
            <p class="text-ink font-bold">Old reviews get revisited.</p>
            <p class="text-ink-soft mt-1">Apps change. Companies get bought. Features get removed. Something that was
              solid two years ago might be a mess now, or vice versa. I go back and check.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Money Section -->
      <section class="mb-12 bg-sun rounded-[24px] p-6 md:p-8 border-[1.5px] border-ink shadow-[4px_5px_0_0_var(--color-ink)]">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4">The Money Thing</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
          Might as well be upfront about this. Some links on the site are affiliate links. You buy something through them,
          I get a cut. Doesn't change what you pay. Standard affiliate model.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          What that doesn't change: my actual opinion. I've turned down partnerships because the product was meh. Passed
          on easy money because I couldn't honestly recommend the thing. The whole point of this site is that I actually
          use what I write about. Shilling garbage would kind of defeat that.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed mt-4">
          The affiliate stuff lets me keep the site running without paywalls or sponsored posts pretending to be reviews.
          Works for me. Hopefully works for you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Topics Section -->
      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-4">What I Cover</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Basically anything a remote worker might need. Project management apps and why most of them are overkill.
          VPNs. Which ones actually work in China, which ones are just marketing. Home office gear that's worth the money
          and stuff that's overpriced garbage.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/85 leading-relaxed">
          Time trackers. Password managers. The best way to set up a standing desk without spending $800.
          Communication tools that won't make your team hate each other. If it helps remote work suck less, I'm probably
          testing it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- CTA Section -->
      <section
          class="text-center bg-sky-light rounded-[32px] p-8 md:p-10 border-[1.5px] border-ink shadow-[5px_6px_0_0_var(--color-ink)]">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink mb-3">Got a Question? Suggestion?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink/85 mb-6">
          Want me to review something specific? Found an error? Or just want to say hey? I actually read these.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact/"
           class="btn-pill btn-ink">
          Get in Touch
        </a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
